                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Capt. Wiltse to Mr.
                            Tracy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January 18, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Via San Francisco, January 28.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>The cabinet was voted out on January 12; another was appointed on January 14, on
                    which date the Queen prorogued the legislature and attempted to proclaim new
                    constitution. At 2 p.m. on January 16 the citizens met and organized a committee
                    of safety. At 4:30 p.m. landed force in accordance with the request of the
                    United States minister plenipotentiary.</p>
                <p>Tuesday (17th) afternoon the Provisional Government was established; the Queen
                    dethroned. The revolution was accomplished without loss of life. Everything is
                    quiet. Commission appointed so as to negotiate terms of annexation to the United
                    States Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiltse.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
